A Rust unit test function named test_dex_loop_with_cpx_and_bne added to cpu.rs, which loads a program into the CPU that initializes X to 8, runs a loop decrementing X until it reaches 3 using CPX and BNE instructions, storing the X register at memory addresses 0x0200 and 0x0201, then asserting that register X and memory locations hold the expected final values.